   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The antecedent of \"which sum shall be known as the 'Direct Payment Settlement Amount'\" is uncertain: it may denote Defendant's own $1,005,233,716 payment or the pooled fund after other institutions' money is added. The figure itself is also written with a decimal point rather than a comma.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.40},
     {"issue": "Paragraphs 9 and 10 make both releases effective \"upon payment of the Direct Payment Settlement Amount by Defendant\", which Defendant cannot do if that term means the pooled sum contributed by all institutions as paragraph 3 appears to define it.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.32}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The Borrower Payment Amount is written \"$1,489,813.925.00\", a figure with two decimal points that cannot be read as written. Eligibility also turns on unstated criteria \"set forth by the State members of the Monitoring Committee\".", "type": 1, "prob": 0.31},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The relief figure is punctuated \"$3.434.000.000\" and the credit entitlement is left entirely to Exhibit D (\"credit towards such obligation as described in Exhibit D\"), so the amount and the measure of satisfaction are both uncertain on the face of the paragraph.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33},
     {"issue": "Paragraph 12 lets a party withdraw for failure to make \"Consumer Relief Payments\" as defined in Exhibit F, a term that does not match the consumer relief obligation as described here, leaving the trigger for withdrawal unclear.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.25}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Shall be enforced in accordance with the authorities provided in the Enforcement Terms\" does not say whether Exhibit E supplies the exclusive route to enforcement or merely one available route.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.36},
     {"issue": "Read with paragraph 13, under which the Court \"retains jurisdiction ... to enforce its terms\", it is unclear whether a party may seek judicial enforcement directly or must first exhaust the Exhibit E process and the Monitor's role under paragraph 7.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.38}
   ]}
]}

